bp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" data=\"[object Object]\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>An internal investigation released late Thursday found former Labor Secretary Lori Chavez-DeRemer allowed harassment of staffers, had an inappropriate relationship with a security aide and used government funds for personal travel.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" data=\"[object Object]\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Released months after Chavez-DeRemer <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/labor-secretary-resigns-after-tumultuous-tenure-21d256e0?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">resigned under a cloud of allegations</a>, the 40-page report by the department’s internal watchdog described a “toxic, intimidating and humiliating” workplace at the federal agency tasked with protecting U.S. workers. The department also didn’t appear to have a policy addressing personal or romantic relationships between supervisors and subordinates, it found.&nbsp;</p>','Business','[\"Lifestyle\",\"Tennis\",\"Soccer\",\"Mental Health\",\"Health\"]',NULL,'Yapa','writer1@gmail.com','Pending review','/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Fthumb_1788611443381.webp',NULL,'[]','5 min read',0,1788611449948,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-09-05 12:30:48','2026-09-05 12:48:18'),('1788611516931','Energy & Utilities Roundup: Market Talk','1788611516931','1559 ET – Crude futures settle higher in a choppy session ahead of the U.S. Labor Day long weekend','closing out a week of gains that saw the resumption of U.S. strikes on Iranian targets and Iranian attacks on shipping. Oil price gains have been tempered by li...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611516931_img_1788611519140_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">closing out a week of gains that saw the resumption of U.S. strikes on Iranian targets and Iranian attacks on shipping. Oil price gains have been tempered by limited flows getting through the Strait of Hormuz, although differences remain on how much oil is making it out. A bigger-than-expected 4.5 million barrel draw in U.S. crude stocks reported midweek by the EIA added upside pressure. WTI settles up 0.2% at $91.48 a barrel, up 9.7% on the week. Brent rises 0.8% to $96.28, or 9.3% higher than a week ago.(anthony.harrup@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Wealth Management\",\"Investing\",\"Designers\",\"Construction\",\"Manufacturing\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Yapa','writer1@gmail.com','Published','/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611516931_img_1788611519140_0.webp',NULL,'[]','5 min read',0,1788612206286,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-09-05 12:32:00','2026-09-05 12:48:18'),('1788611589238','Auto & Transport Roundup: Market Talk','1788611589238','903 ET – Volkswagen’s restructuring agreement is a major positive surprise','proves the company can implement its transformation program despite complex governance and labor constraints, Bank of America Securities analysts Horst Schneide...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611589238_img_1788611592820_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">proves the company can implement its transformation program despite complex governance and labor constraints, Bank of America Securities analysts Horst Schneider and Stephen Benhamou write. Ahead of the meeting, media reports had suggested an escalating confrontation with labor and state representatives, potentially culminating in legal action or an extraordinary general meeting, the bank says. “Against this backdrop, we believe few expected a unanimous agreement.” The plan envisages around 50,000 additional job reductions globally by 2030, taking the total number to 100,000, but the detailed measures still need to be agreed. It is therefore not yet clear when restructuring provisions will be booked, but the bank estimates gross charges of up to 10 billion euros, probably spread over several years. Shares rise 7.6%. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Energy\",\"Culture\",\"Architecture\",\"Arts\",\"Music\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Yapa','writer1@gmail.com','Published','/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611589238_img_1788611592820_0.webp',NULL,'[]','5 min read',0,1788612198200,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-09-05 12:33:14','2026-09-05 12:48:18'),('1788611658413','Basic Materials Roundup: Market Talk','1788611658413','1437 ET – Gold futures fell as U.S. payrolls increased well above expectations in August, pushing up short-term Treasury yields and raising expectations of a possible September Fed hike.','President Trump, however, called for lower interest rates following the employment report. “A resilient labor market would give the Fed permission to move rates...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611658413_img_1788611661803_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;President Trump, however, called for lower interest rates following the employment report. “A resilient labor market would give the Fed permission to move rates higher at the September meeting if upcoming August inflation data does not show continued improvement, but that political pressure to maintain 