t\",\"Tech\"]',NULL,'Oshidi','writer@gmail.com','Pending review','/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Fthumb_1788612491098.webp',NULL,'[]','5 min read',0,1788612498226,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-09-05 12:48:18','2026-09-05 12:57:27'),('1788613042225','Volkswagen’s Peace Deal With Unions Sets Up Fresh Battles to Come','1788613042225','To win approval to cut thousands more jobs, automaker kicked questions about factory closures and governance down the road',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788613042225_img_1788613045653_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;','World Politics','[\"Currencies\",\"Economy\",\"Interest Rates\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Innovation\"]',NULL,'Oshidi','writer@gmail.com','Pending review','/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Fthumb_1788613042225.webp',NULL,'[]','5 min read',0,1788613047945,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-09-05 12:57:27','2026-09-05 13:02:42'),('1788613358967','Computer Makers Are Selling Fewer PCs at Higher Prices. So Far, It’s Working','1788613358967','The trend is being driven by the shortage of memory chips, and accompanying soaring costs, stemming from the AI infrastructure buildout','Computer makers have been forced into an interesting trade off: Sell fewer PCs at far higher prices.The trend is being driven by the same shortage of memory chi...','<section class=\"ef4qpkp0 css-1579sa9-Container e11lw8gk0\" style=\"width: 620px; position: relative; display: flow-root; view-timeline: --main-scroll-tracker; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\"><figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788613358967_img_1788613361477_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" data=\"[object Object]\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\">&nbsp;</span>Computer makers have been forced into an interesting trade off: Sell fewer PCs at far higher prices.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" data=\"[object Object]\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The trend is being driven by the same shortage of memory chips, and accompanying soaring costs, stemming from the massive buildout of artificial-intelligence infrastructure. The bottleneck has trickled down to personal computers, which has sent prices higher, at the expense of units sold.</p></section><p class=\"css-16aepit e1jdulti0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; position: absolute; z-index: -1; top: 0px; left: -15000px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Hel